Search docs + annotations by meaning and words (maps to memory.search)

Usage: tasqx memory search [OPTIONS] <QUERY>...

Arguments:
  <QUERY>...
          Search words. Matched as phrases, so hyphens and dots are safe.
          
          Deliberately NOT named `filter`: this is FTS text, not the filter DSL, so the argv hyphen pre-pass must leave it alone.

Options:
      --json
          Print the raw JSON API result instead of the human table

      --limit <LIMIT>
          Max hits (default 10)

      --scope <SCOPE>
          What to search (default: all)
          
          [possible values: all, docs, annotations]

      --theme <THEME>
          Theme name (built-in nord|gruvbox|dracula|solarized|mono, or a user file). Overrides $TASQX_THEME and the config file (DESIGN.md §8)

      --raw
          Treat the query as raw FTS5 syntax (prefix*, AND/OR, columns). Words only: it searches as `--mode lexical`, and the engine refuses it beside a mode that runs meaning

      --socket <SOCKET>
          Local socket / named-pipe address of a tasqx daemon. Overrides $TASQX_SOCK. When a daemon is reachable, one-shot commands route through it (single writer); otherwise they run in-process. A set $TASQX_DB naming a different store than that daemon's is refused. Also selects the address for `daemon` and `watch`

      --mode <MODE>
          How to match (default: hybrid, meaning and words fused; lexical forces exact words)
          
          [possible values: hybrid, lexical, semantic]

      --no-daemon
          Never route through a daemon; always run one-shot in-process (the pre-daemon behaviour). Escape hatch for scripts

      --min-similarity <N>
          The floor a match by meaning must reach, 0 to 1 (default 0.30)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
